  "title": "RC - the Room Criteria",
  "description": "The Room Criteria (RC) is used to measure background noise in buildings for frequencies ranging 16 to 4000 Hz. RC requires a determination of the mid-frequency average level and the perceived balance between high and low frequency sound.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# RC - the Room Criteria\n\nThe Room Criteria (RC) is used to measure background noise in buildings over frequencies ranging **16 Hz** to **4000 Hz**.\n\nRC requires a determination of the mid-frequency average level and the perceived balance between high and low frequency sound.\n\n## Neutral (N) Criteria\nThe levels in the octave bands centered at 500 Hz and below must not exceed the octave-band levels of the reference spectrum by more than 5 dB at any point in the range; the levels in the octave bands centered at 1000 Hz and above must not exceed the octave-band level of the reference spectrum by more than 3 dB at any point in the range."
    },
